Package: rssiradar
Version: 1.3.1
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: RSSI Radar maintainer
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.38), libgcc-s1 (>= 4.0), libqt6core6t64 (>= 6.4.0),
 libqt6gui6t64 (>= 6.4.0), libqt6widgets6t64 (>= 6.1.2), libstdc++6 (>= 13.1),
 libbluetooth3
Recommends: iw, network-manager
Suggests: tcpdump
Installed-Size: 3400
Section-Description: science
Description:
 Passive WiFi and Bluetooth radiometric motion sensing.
 .
 RSSI Radar senses motion passively using real raw sockets: AF_PACKET with
 radiotap header parsing for WiFi, and an AF_BLUETOOTH HCI socket for LE
 advertising reports. There is no simulated-data path in the program -- every
 reported value derives from frames a real radio received, and hardware that
 cannot deliver is reported explicitly rather than faked.
 .
 The signal chain is a log-distance path-loss inversion, Savitzky-Golay
 smoothing, adaptive CFAR with entropy and chi-square change detection,
 extended Kalman and particle filters for state, and a Welch averaged
 periodogram that converts the envelope beat frequency into radial velocity
 via v = f_beat * lambda.
 .
 Eight operating presets ship with the program, from breath detection to
 fast intrusion and strict laboratory baselines. Configuration is JSON and can
 be saved and reloaded from the interface.
 .
 Note: switching the interface to monitor mode requires real root, because it
 drives iw and NetworkManager over D-Bus. The package grants CAP_NET_RAW and
 CAP_NET_ADMIN so that passive managed-mode capture and the hardware probe work
 without it.
